1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,734
In this town, everyone lives in one building.

2
00:00:03,627 --> 00:00:04,786
One hundred floors.

3
00:00:05,427 --> 00:00:08,101
The richer you are, the higher you live.

4
00:00:08,993 --> 00:00:10,758
I live on floor two.

5
00:00:11,327 --> 00:00:13,092
Just above the parking garage.

6
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:16,637
Every elevator in the building has the same buttons.

7
00:00:17,627 --> 00:00:19,089
One to one hundred.

8
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:21,022
Every elevator except one.

9
00:00:21,493 --> 00:00:24,471
The old one, at the end of the hall.

10
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,831
It has a button nobody talks about.

11
00:00:28,627 --> 00:00:29,180
Zero.

12
00:00:30,527 --> 00:00:31,989
Grandma says it's broken.

13
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,528
Grandma also says never press it.

14
00:00:35,193 --> 00:00:36,958
So obviously, I pressed it.

15
00:00:37,527 --> 00:00:38,686
The doors closed.

16
00:00:39,327 --> 00:00:40,486
The lights flickered.

17
00:00:41,127 --> 00:00:42,892
And the elevator went down.

18
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,225
For a very long time.

19
00:00:45,793 --> 00:00:48,468
When the doors opened, I saw a lobby.

20
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,519
Exactly like ours.

21
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,016
Same plants.

22
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:53,816
Same carpet.

23
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:55,616
Same people.

24
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,325
But everyone was standing still.

25
00:00:58,893 --> 00:01:00,382
Staring at the elevator.

26
00:01:00,827 --> 00:01:01,380
Waiting.

27
00:01:02,727 --> 00:01:05,704
A man in a suit walked up to me.

28
00:01:06,693 --> 00:01:09,073
He looked exactly like the building manager.

29
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,928
But his smile was too wide.

30
00:01:12,593 --> 00:01:14,662
"Welcome to floor zero," he said.

31
00:01:15,327 --> 00:01:17,395
"We've been waiting for a volunteer."

32
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:19,825
"Volunteer for what?" I asked.

33
00:01:20,393 --> 00:01:24,583
"For the swap. One of us goes up. One of you stays down."

34
00:01:25,993 --> 00:01:28,062
Behind him, a boy stepped forward.

35
00:01:28,727 --> 00:01:30,189
He had my hair.

36
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:31,516
My hoodie.

37
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:33,316
My face.

38
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,328
I ran back into the elevator.

39
00:01:36,993 --> 00:01:38,152
I pressed two.

40
00:01:38,793 --> 00:01:39,952
Two. Two. Two.

41
00:01:40,593 --> 00:01:42,662
The doors closed just in time.

42
00:01:43,327 --> 00:01:45,395
At least I think they did.

43
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:48,734
Because this morning, Grandma made my favorite breakfast.

44
00:01:49,627 --> 00:01:51,392
And I didn't like it.

